  "statement": "\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCan you find a Pythagorean triple with 17 as the largest number? Use the \u003ci\u003eList \u003c/i\u003efeature on your calculator to find the value of 17\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e – \u003ci\u003ex\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e for \u003ci\u003ex\u003c/i\u003e \u003d 1, 2, 3, .... If you find a perfect square, you\u0027ve got a Pythagorean triple!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e",
  "statementFigure": null,
  "question": null,
  "widgetSlot": null,
  "steps": [
